														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-240771">
									

<p>Wow, thanks man.</p>
<p>1) As for the extra souls in a single body, you'd most likely get a type of extreme multiple personality disorder, with the souls vying for dominance of the body. The stronger, or more enthusiastic ones would be at the forefront most of the time, and the weaker, apathetic ones would be dormant more often.</p>
<p>2) The item would become sentient, but behave like a ghost, in the sense that it would "haunt" the surrounding area.</p>
<p>3) For artificial intelligence…. Well, that's a whole can of worms there. It depends on the question, can a machine created by man possess a soul? Not an SCP machine mind you, just a machine. So I'm not exactly sure about that one myself. Possibly if the program was one that was engineered to learn, to have emotions and feelings and memories and such.</p>
<p>4) Well, I'd guess you'd have either a single person in charge of two bodies, a pair of people who cannot mentally carry on without the other, or some mixture of the two.</p>
<p>Like I said, thanks!</p>

							</div>

								
					
